1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
The first time you open WildObserve,
it asks you to create the administrator account.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,500
You can set it up with your Google account,
or with your name, email, and a password.

3
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:18,800
Here we click Set up with Google and finish in the web browser.
WildObserve carries on by itself.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Once you're signed in, make your first project.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,800
Click Add a folder... and choose the folder
that holds your camera-trap images.

6
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:38,500
Subfolders are included, and each folder of images is a deployment.
Your images stay where they are: WildObserve doesn't copy them.

7
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,000
Give the project a name, then click Make project.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,500
The project opens and finds your images.
